Arc Ecosystem Tier List 📘

If you're hunting for opportunities on Arc, don't start with the apps everyone is already farming.

I’d look at Arc through 4 different angles:

AI agents → Payments → Trading infra → Launch opportunities

Here are the names worth digging into 👇

1. AI agents are probably the most interesting sector right now

@memoAI_ARC
Natural-language payment assistant.

@nexorafi
Agent wallets, spending limits, x402, and escrow.

@gigawork_arc
Agent marketplace where payment is released only after the task is completed.

@uzenlabs
Identity layer for autonomous agents.

@ProofStream_
USDC payroll that unlocks based on completed work.

If the AI x crypto narrative keeps heating up, apps like these could attract attention fast.

Simple rule:

Never give a new agent access to your main wallet.

---

2. Arc looks like it’s making a serious bet on stablecoins and payments

This is one category I’d watch more closely than NFTs or gaming.

@koshmoney
Stablecoin neobank + cross-border payments.

@BlockradarHQ
Wallet infrastructure for fintechs.

@Hinkal_protocol
Privacy wallet + confidential settlement.

@cyclesmoney
Payments infrastructure.

@ArrelTechnology
Payment rails.

If Arc really wants to become a chain for internet money, some of the earliest winners could come from this group.

---

3. Want to find tokens early? Watch the trading infra first

Instead of waiting for tokens to show up on major DEXs, look at where tokens are being created and where liquidity starts forming.

@NebulaPad
A launchpad starting to show up on ArcLens.

@Fliptfun
Bonding curve + fee sharing.

@Arguspad
Launchpad + AMM.

@synthra_finance
AMM + aggregator + launchpad.

@onmidotfun
Multichain launchpad expanding into Arc.

This category carries more risk, but it’s also where new markets often appear first.

---

4. Don’t ignore the smaller DEXs

Liquidity rarely stays in one place forever.

@TowerExchange
Stablecoin aggregator.

@lunexfinance
StableSwap for USDC, EURC, and USDT.

@lunya_io
AMM + curve launches + CCTP bridge.

@Xylonet_
Stablecoin-focused exchange.

@peachlfg
Aggregator + token launch surface.

@swaparc_app
Stablecoin swaps + a private payments angle.

No need to deposit much.

At the start, the goal should simply be:

→ Test the product
→ Create interactions
→ Track volume
→ See where liquidity is moving

---

5. NFTs and gaming are optional bets

@arcblockborn
NFT collection timed around mainnet.

@TurtzWTF
Browser game + P2E.

@PlayMossling
Gaming ecosystem on Arc.

I wouldn’t prioritize this category over payments, agents, or launch infra.

But if Arc gets a strong retail rotation, NFT and gaming projects can move very fast.

Bookmark this list

